<BaseLayout title="The Notch in a Voltage Source — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>The Notch in a Voltage Source</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Add an output capacitor and the stiffness curve stops being monotonic. At
    the frequency where the capacitor and the inductor branch cancel, the
    supply is at its weakest — and the resistance that damps that notch is the
    same resistance that costs stiffness everywhere below it, and burns the
    heat. The load step on the right is the same story in the time domain: the
    sag is the low-frequency asymptote, the ringing is the notch.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
